00:34:48.489 --> 00:34:50.219
In fact, I think
there's actually even,

00:34:50.219 --> 00:34:54.489
on istio.io there's a countdown
clock for the exact time--

00:34:54.489 --> 00:34:55.380
[CHEERING]

00:34:55.380 --> 00:34:58.990
Exactly, right, so 1.0,
that's a pretty big deal.

00:34:58.990 --> 00:35:02.950
We also have managed Istio on
GKE, which is going into alpha.

00:35:02.950 --> 00:35:06.690
So if people are
interested in maybe a way

00:35:06.690 --> 00:35:11.220
to have a play with Istio in a
GKE environment, let us know.

00:35:11.220 --> 00:35:12.750
Please reach out.

00:35:12.750 --> 00:35:15.570
We're actually taking
people on that side.

00:35:15.570 --> 00:35:18.409
And we also have some
Apigee API integration.

00:35:18.409 --> 00:35:19.950
NANDAN SRIDHAR: Yes,
and that's going

00:35:19.950 --> 00:35:21.940
to be the GA the same day.

00:35:21.940 --> 00:35:23.640
It's just 1.0.

00:35:23.640 --> 00:35:25.850
So you guys can look up GitHub.

00:35:25.850 --> 00:35:27.230
It's also open source.

